# state: any   (golden 9153c63300da promoted 2026-10-11; lane.savestate433)
# Grand Theft Auto III (5454000E): one route, first-run or on the golden.
# PATHFOUND by pathfind.py on the Nova, 2026-10-11 (lane.gtaroutes1011
# session 1034707; path recorded to pathknow/paths/5454000E.json, gameplay
# reached in 2.2 min / 14 steps).
#
#   Loading icon -> several Rockstar/publisher-logo screens and a black
#   frame (non-interactive) -> intro credits video (A skips it) -> title
#   screen (A starts a new game here too, same as START) -> betrayal/
#   bridge-explosion cutscene (A skips it) -> second cutscene (A skips it)
#   -> Portland street, Claude on foot, full HUD (health, money, radar,
#   wanted level, weapon icon).
#
# gtawedge1012 (2026-10-12): confirmation 1-1791785131-lane.local-2109239
# booted faster than this route assumed -- its first 4 A presses (55-70s)
# already reached the street with no HUD up yet (route-frames/
# 234745-introskip.png). The blind `press START` that followed landed
# in-game and opened the PAUSE menu instead of the title screen; the next
# A-trains then answered "start a new game? / Cancel" over and over
# (route-frames/234826-cut1.png, 234849-cut2.png, 234855-gameplay.png all
# show that same dialog). `mark gameplay` fired into that dialog at
# 23:48:55; real play did not begin until ~23:51:56, once the regular play
# loop's own LX/A presses happened to land on OK. So: no START (A alone
# both skips and starts, as the run above proves), and the mark is gated
# on a `waitfor` of the in-play weapon icon -- a region that is a hand/fist
# box only once Claude is actually on foot under control, never during the
# loading/logo/title/cutscene/pause-menu states (scored 65-106 on those
# frames vs 0-10 on real gameplay frames from that same run; see NOTES.md).
# A timeout here aborts the route, which is correct: a run that never
# reached play must not score.
#
# The A-train is a press 5 s apart (as gta-sa.route): loading time differs
# between runs, and an A that lands on a loading/logo screen is a no-op.
# Player control: pathfind's probe step moved the player with LY up. The
# play pattern runs, sprints, steers and turns the camera; it never
# presses Y, START or BACK.
#
wait 55
repeat 4 {
    press A 300
    wait 5
}
shot introskip
repeat 12 {
    press A 300
    wait 5
}
shot pregameplay
waitfor fist-hud 60 1020,88,140,130 20
mark gameplay
repeat forever {
    repeat 4 {
        axis LY min
        press A 200
        wait 1.5
        axis LX max
        wait 1
        axis LX mid
        press A 200
        wait 1.5
        axis LX min
        wait 1
        axis LX mid
        axis RX max
        wait 0.5
        axis RX mid
        wait 1
        axis LY mid
        wait 0.5
    }
    # wedge escape (gtawedge1012): identical loop to gta-vc.route. The
    # inner body alone drifts heading right only 0.5s of RX max per ~10s
    # cycle (see that route's comment for the Vice City wedge this fixes);
    # this title runs the same body, so it gets the same escape.
    axis LY max
    wait 2
    axis RX max
    wait 1.5
    axis LX mid
    axis LY mid
    axis RX mid
}
